=== NEXT SESSION: BINDLESS TEXTURE DESCRIPTOR ALLOCATION ===

1. POPULATE TEXTURE DESCRIPTOR INDICES
   - In upload_texture_to_gpu(): assign next available index in bindless sampler2D array
   - Store mapping: m_texture_allocation[TextureHandle] = descriptor_index
   - Validate descriptor index doesn't exceed descriptor pool size

2. IMPLEMENT MATERIAL ALLOCATION
   - In upload_material_to_gpu():
     * Call upload_texture_to_gpu() for all material textures (albedo, normal, metallic, roughness, ao)
     * Collect descriptor indices for each texture
     * Create MaterialAllocation struct with indices
     * Store in m_material_allocations map
   - Add m_material_allocations map to RenderResourceManager header

3. UPDATE DESCRIPTOR SETS FOR BINDLESS ARRAY
   - After textures are populated, write descriptor set with VkImageViews at assigned indices
   - Call vkUpdateDescriptorSets() to bind textures to sampler2D array
   - Ensure proper synchronization before rendering

4. RENDERING INTEGRATION
   - MeshAllocation references MaterialHandle
   - During render: lookup MaterialAllocation for material descriptor indices
   - Pass descriptor indices to shader via push constants or UBO
   - Update shaders to use nonuniformEXT(material_index) for dynamic indexing

5. TEST ASSET PIPELINE
   - Load .obj model with materials
   - Verify texture descriptor indices assigned correctly
   - Verify MaterialAllocation created properly
   - Render and confirm bindless texture lookups work 